== (3) the Hankel form of the depth: linear complexity of (2^(d_k)) = odd-step depth + 1 ==
  LC(2^(d_k(n)), continued along the 1-cycle) = d_odd(n) + 1 for all odd n <= 3000: True 
  reading: Kronecker -- the generating function sum 2^(d_k) z^k is rational iff the Hankel determinants vanish from
  some size on; the odd-step depth is that size minus one; a divergent orbit would have infinite Hankel rank
